   ],
   "ms": [
    [
     "58",
     "2",
     "B1 for 58<br>B1 for <i>alternate segment theorem</i> (angle between tangent and chord = angle in the alternate segment)"
    ],
    [
     "116",
     "1",
     "B1<br>FT 2 \u00d7 their (a)"
    ]
   ],
   "sols": [
    [
     [
      "<i>SA</i> is the tangent and <i>AB</i> is the chord, so angle <i>SAB</i> = 58\u00b0 is a tangent\u2013chord angle.",
      ""
     ],
     [
      "<i>C</i> lies in the segment on the other side of chord <i>AB</i>.",
      "the alternate segment"
     ],
     [
      "Angle <i>ACB</i> = <b>58\u00b0</b>",
      "alternate segment theorem: the angle between a tangent and a chord equals the angle in the alternate segment"
     ]
    ],
    [
     [
      "Angle <i>ACB</i> is at the circumference and angle <i>AOB</i> is at the centre, both on arc <i>AB</i>.",
      ""
     ],
     [
      "Angle <i>AOB</i> = 2 \u00d7 58 = <b>116\u00b0</b>",
      "the angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference"
     ]
    ]
   ]
